PURPOSE   Two frozen-oracle cases can never pass and the registered end-goal
          N=M is unattainable with this oracle. Cause: assert_case matches with
          'case "$obs" in $want)' and bash treats a '|' introduced by parameter
          expansion as a LITERAL character, not alternation. The affected calls:
          tools/mori-silence-cases.sh:455  assert_case ledger-missing-not-silent 'not-open|unavailable' 0 0
          tools/mori-silence-cases.sh:613  assert_case report-future-no-close 'progressing-weak|silent' auto auto
          Counterfactual: byte-identical copy with ONLY the matcher block replaced
          by '[[ "$obs" =~ ^($want)$ ]]' — the intended alternation semantics.

---- bash semantics probe (this host) ----
GNU bash, version 5.3.15(1)-release (x86_64-pc-linux-gnu)
  expansion probe: LITERAL-no-match
  literal probe:    MATCH-literal-string
  => alternation must be SYNTACTIC in the case pattern or a regex test; an
     expanded '|' matches nothing but a literal '|'.

---- patch (unified diff: frozen -> counterfactual) ----
--- tools/mori-silence-cases.sh	2026-10-15 12:40:11.230655493 -0300
+++ /tmp/mori-receipts-r3/oracle-cf.sh	2026-10-15 13:55:28.053952169 -0300
@@ -359,10 +359,8 @@
   fi
 
   local ok=1 why=''
-  case "$obs" in
-    $want) : ;;
-    *) ok=0; why="state want [$want] got [$obs] via $api";;
-  esac
+  if [[ "$obs" =~ ^($want)$ ]]; then :;
+  else ok=0; why="state want [$want] got [$obs] via $api"; fi
   local wff=$wf
   [ "$wf" = auto ] && { [ "$obs" = silent ] && wff=1 || wff=0; }
   if [ "$fobs" -ne "$wff" ]; then
---- end patch ----

